was super bowl week in houston and when  the reports first came out we were like  what  john lynch going to become a general  manager and the first thought was this  could either be john elway or matt  millen and so far it's closer to elway  the good old way always had some good  and some bad in his nine years with the  broncos but it really has turned around  in year three for john lynch and it  wasn't that long ago that there was talk  about how lynch and shanahan maybe it's  not going to work and they had the 4 and  12 season last year and maybe the heat's  going to be on one or both of them this  year notwithstanding the six-year  contracts fully guaranteed that both  have but it really has worked out and it  always takes time everybody wants that  quick fix in the nfl especially when you  see a team like the 49ers turn around  from four and 12 one year to super bowl  the next but it does take time to get  the players in place to run the offense  and the defense that kyle shanahan  envisioned and john lynch did a hell of  a job finding the right players to run  that team the way shanahan wants it  sometimes he ask a question when you're  talking to somebody and you really don't  know what direction he's going to go  uh and i did not know that story  and i said to myself that's that's an  incredible story and how about when he  says you know i basically didn't sleep  for like the next four nights  um  and  one of the reasons why i think john  lynch  is really really good at this job  and again why  we could get in a long argument it'd be  a fun podcast one day for me and you to  do  but  i happen to think that what ruined matt  millen  in detroit  was  and we could argue about this a long  time he was basically forced to pick  joey harrington he didn't want to pick  joey harrington but in retrospect now  what has been the absolute key for the  49ers the key is getting the quarterback  who can win games when your team is not  playing great  getting a quarterback who can overcome  some obstacles that's what jimmy  garoppolo has done this year and so to  me  every general manager who works why is  john elway getting such a grace period  in denver  because he convinced peyton manning  eight years ago along with pat bolan who  was in declining health but he also  helped he convinced peyton manning to go  to denver  and he got a super bowl out of it as it  turns out  but in my opinion it's all about the  quarterback however that happened and  one day it's either going to be in the  john lynch book or the bill belichick  book  how jimmy garoppolo landed in san  francisco for a two  you know because he could have gotten  more elsewhere but that has been the  whole key getting a quarterback somehow  some way lynch and shanahan got that  done and that to me has made all the  difference  but it's amazing that in the playoffs  jimmy garoppolo has essentially become  bob greasy right throwing the ball eight  times in the nfc championship game and  who knows how many times he'll throw the  ball against the chiefs in the super  bowl peter i think one of the keys here  and to the extent that there is anything  about the 49ers that other teams can  copy  i think the 49ers with shanahan and  lynch have done a great job of finding  guys who are natural born roughnecks who  don't need the reps that no longer are  available in hitting and blocking and  tackling to the ground football has gone  dramatically in the direction away from  full contact at practices they're trying  to eliminate concussions you do that in  part by having practices not nearly as  intense as they used to be so what  happens what happens is you get to a  game and patrick holmes is running to  the end zone and nobody knows how to  tackle him i think the 49ers have found  guys on the offensive and defensive side  of the ball who don't need that they are  natural born badasses who will go out  there and execute without hesitation  without practice reps they just know  how to overpower you like a george  kittle he's the epitome of it the  defense is the same way but especially  with that running game why all of a  sudden are the 49ers cracking the code  on the running game because defenses  don't know how to tackle anymore and  they don't know how to fight off the  blocks anymore because they don't do it  full speed like they used to they found  guys who don't need to do it full speed  in practice i think that's been the very  subtle key to this and that's the  challenge for other teams find guys like  that who can match that brawn match that  will match that violence in games  against the 49ers  mike there's one other guy who we don't  talk about with the san francisco 49ers  who absolutely unequivocally we should  one day he will be a general manager in  the nfl his name is adam peters and he's  their personnel guy their chief college  guy  and i remember i was in the draft room  in night in 2017 before their first nfl  draft uh as a as a team you know lynch  and shanahan and adam peters sitting  over to one side  and they did something in the fifth  round of that draft and they took george  kittle that was by far  the best pick in terms of value in three  years that they've run this team and the  reason that they were able to get george  kittle in the fifth round is very simple  he was a devalued player at iowa the  coaching staff didn't really love him he  hadn't produced a lot  uh  and and i think he came to the nfl  as a real you know on the come guy and  the 49ers saw how much he loved football  and how much they thought he could  project to this level and that's exactly  what they've done  so a don't forget adam peters when we  talk about shanahan and lynch and b the  other part that i think is really  really important it isn't just getting  the nick bosas and and all those guys  even though they've spent huge draft  capital on the front when you spend huge  draft capital on the front you're gonna  have to find  fred warner george kittle later in the  draft you're gonna have to find raheem  mostert on the undrafted free agent  scrap heap after he's been cut by 64  teams that is what the 49ers have done  exceedingly well  and really the guy who's responsible  most directly and clearly for the 49ers  being in the super bowl i mean plenty of  guys have their hand in it but dre  greenlaw  not fading to his left  but crashing back to the right to get to  jacob hollister and keep him out of the  end zone because peter if hollister  scores that touchdown at the closing  moment of week 17 and the seahawks beat  the 49ers the 49ers are the five seed  and look maybe they would have won on  the road in philly they probably would  have like seattle did but then you gotta  go maybe to uh green bay and beat the 49  or beat the packers rather at lambeau  field or maybe have to go back to  seattle at some point i mean it's a far  different road and you don't get your  bye week that i think they desperately  needed and greenlaw doesn't make that  play we may be talking about the  seahawks or the packers or somebody else  in super bowl 54 not the san francisco  49ers  hey there's no question about it and  mike i i do think  sometimes when i think of the nfl's  playoff system and i think how  absolutely close that is how painfully  close that was for the seattle seahawks  because obviously if their home  you know for the first  week or to if they have a buy and then  they're home for either one or two weeks  how much of a huge difference this could  have  would have made in the nfc playoffs and  maybe  who makes it to the super bowl from the  nfc the one thing about  all of this  and i on one hand i think it's  tremendously unfair but on the other  hand  that's what makes a game like this that  we're showing right now a play like that  so incredibly spectacular  because  a play like that three inches can make  the difference in whether you win a  super bowl and that's not being overly  dramatic it's absolutely true  same thing for the chiefs though if the  patriots don't  fail to beat the dolphins in week 17 how  different that would have configured the  afc field and the chiefs would have been  the three seed and they wouldn't have  had a buy they would have had to face  the titans right out of the gates who  knows how it would have gone as a wild  card match up and then their reward  would have been they go to new england  for the divisional round and they're on  the road for potentially the afc  championship game in baltimore if they  had been able to hold serve uh et cetera  et cetera so uh it did really you know  when it comes down to that last couple  of weeks of the season to determine the  playoff tree we know most of the playoff  teams but those spots at the top of the  playoff tree we're reminded again and  again peter how critical they are you  also talk to joe staley after the nfc  championship game he is a link back to  the super bowl 47 49ers team uh  how confident was he after everything  that the 49ers have gone through since  super bowl 47 that he was ever going to  see another super bowl  i asked him flat out did you ever think  he'd be back here right now and he said  no i didn't  but he said the first time i sat and  listened to kyle shanahan i said hey  this guy is really really good we could  get back there and so i think that is  when  a coach can make all the difference and  look joe staley has been relatively  unscathed injury-wise in his career i'm  sure he's thinking hey  i make i don't even know what he makes  10 12 million whatever he makes  i'll make 30 million for the next three  years 35 million and i'll just sort of  slip into retirement and i will have had  a really good career uh you know played  in the super bowl and all that  but i think that kyle shanahan woke the  echoes in san francisco there's no doubt  about it and mike  i can't help but thinking  just think now if you're john elway  watching that game the other night  and you think about the coaching  decision that you had in front of you in  2017  and you ask yourself  i had kyle shanahan in the final two  did i really make the call that i made  because i think john elway will always  say going into the 2017 coach process he  had his mind made up that's one of the  things that he did differently with vic  fangio i'm going in with an open mind  i have no preconceived notions and in  2019 he made a better decision i think a  smarter decision than he made in 2017.  to take it back to where we started  though who's to say that kyle shanahan  and john elway would have formed that  working relationship that shanahan and  lynch have put together and it's worked  out perfectly and remember at the time  the thinking was shanahan was going to  have a hard time finding a gm  who is currently working for another  team because shanahan's running the show  and you can't  make that higher of a guy unless you're  giving him the full gm powers and  authorities and that's what made lynch a  perfect alternative and it was amazing  and i still remember how that just was  out of the blue and it was one of those  things where at first you say this makes  no sense but the more you thought about  it well i could see this making sense  and here we are three years later super  bowl 54 shanahan and lynch and the 49ers  back uh trying to win it for the first  time in 25 years  hi i'm mike tarico and thanks for  watching make sure to hit subscribe for  the latest news and highlights from nbc  sports

